`ensureFTSIndexViaExecutor` recorded the `(repoId, table)` ensure-key on every code path, including the catch-all branch. A single transient `CREATE_FTS_INDEX` failure (e.g. lock contention on first query after MCP server start) therefore disabled BM25 for that repo for the lifetime of the process — silently, since the query path turns FTS errors into `[]`.

### Changes

- **`gitnexus/src/core/search/bm25-index.ts`** — Move `ensuredPoolFTS.add(key)` into the two success branches: `CREATE_FTS_INDEX` succeeded, or it failed with `'already exists'`. All other errors leave the key unset and emit a `console.warn` with `repoId` / table / index / message so the failure is no longer invisible.
- **`gitnexus/src/core/lbug/pool-adapter.ts`** — Add an `addPoolCloseListener(listener) → disposer` registry and fire registered listeners from `closeOne` *after* `pool.delete(repoId)`. Listener exceptions are isolated so teardown always completes.
- **`gitnexus/src/core/search/bm25-index.ts`** — Lazily register a pool-close listener (idempotent, on first MCP-pool-backed query) that calls a new exported `invalidateEnsuredFTSForRepo(repoId)` so LRU eviction / idle close / explicit `closeLbug` drop the matching ensure-state instead of letting it outlive the pool that produced it.
- **Tests** — `gitnexus/test/unit/bm25-search.test.ts` adds four regression cases: transient CREATE failure → second call retries (5 CREATEs again); `'already exists'` is cached (0 CREATEs on retry); explicit `invalidateEnsuredFTSForRepo` clears entries; pool-close listener invalidates only the closed repo, leaving siblings intact.

### Before / after

```ts
// before — key cached on EVERY path, including transient failures
} catch (e: any) {
  const msg = String(e?.message ?? '');
  if (!msg.includes('already exists')) {
    // swallow
  }
}
ensuredPoolFTS.add(key); // ← poisons the cache on failure

// after — cache only on confirmed success
try {
  await executor(`CALL CREATE_FTS_INDEX(...)`);
  ensuredPoolFTS.add(key);
} catch (e: any) {
  const msg = String(e?.message ?? '');
  if (msg.includes('already exists')) {
    ensuredPoolFTS.add(key);
  } else {
    console.warn(`[gitnexus] FTS index ensure failed for repo "${repoId}" ...`);
    // key left unset → next query retries
  }
}
```

### Notes

- CLI/pipeline FTS path (`lbug-adapter.ts`) is untouched; this only affects the MCP-pool path.
- No retry/backoff added — first-retry-works is sufficient per the issue; repeated failures still fall through to `[]` and re-warn.
- No schema, MCP contract, or persistence changes.

